---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Poetry - Claire Nyquist"
    description="Poetry by Claire Nyquist. Coming soon: Mummies & Wildflowers, a collection of poems about birth, bodies, nature, love, and the end."
    image="/images/gifs/poetry-poster.webp"
>
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8">
        <!-- Hero Section -->
        <div class="text-center mb-12">
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl name-gradient mb-6">Poetry</h1>
        </div>

        <!-- Book Section -->
        <div
            class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row items-center lg:items-start justify-center gap-10 lg:gap-16 mb-16"
        >
            <!-- The proof copy, flipping through -->
            <div class="book-video w-full max-w-lg lg:max-w-xl flex-shrink-0">
                <!-- Plain video everywhere; if autoplay is blocked (low
                     power mode), the poster frame stands in. -->
                <video
                    src="/videos/poetry.mp4"
                    poster="/images/gifs/poetry-poster.webp"
                    autoplay
                    muted
                    loop
                    playsinline
                    preload="auto"
                    aria-label="Hands flipping through a printed hardcover proof copy of the poetry book Mummies & Wildflowers on a wooden table."
                    width="1080"
                    height="1270"
                    class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg shadow-lg"
                ></video>
            </div>

            <!-- Coming soon + blurb -->
            <div class="max-w-md lg:pt-8 text-center lg:text-left">
                <p
                    class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-blue-600 mb-3"
                >
                    Coming soon
                </p>
                <h2
                    class="font-space-grotesk text-3xl md:text-4xl text-gray-900 mb-2"
                >
                    Mummies &amp; Wildflowers
                </h2>
                <p class="text-gray-500 italic mb-8">poems</p>
                <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                    Spanning four years of Minnesota weather, Mummies &amp;
                    Wildflowers moves through a full circle of seasons and
                    comes out the other side in bloom.
                </p>
                <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                    These are poems that hold two things at once and refuse to
                    choose: the preserved dead and the flower, the grief and
                    the appetite, the lover and the microscope, the cold breeze
                    and the reason to roll the window down anyway.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- The poem from the back cover. Verbatim from the
             manuscript; each line is its own element so the breaks
             survive, with a hanging indent so a wrapped long line reads
             as a wrap and not as a new line. -->
        <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto pb-4">
            <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-blue-600 mb-3">
                From the back cover
            </p>
            <h2
                class="font-space-grotesk text-2xl md:text-3xl text-gray-900 mb-6"
            >
                Reprieve
            </h2>
            <div class="poem text-gray-700">
                <p>They may say it’s strange to get married in a cemetery</p>
                <p>But it’s beautiful here</p>
                <p>So we dance in the face of death</p>
                <p>Here we celebrate in the company of the departed</p>
                <p>With a sugar skull and a bundle of marigolds</p>
                <p>We’re all just ash on reprieve</p>
                <p>We’re all just nibbles for bacteria in the end</p>
                <p>But we’ve got each other</p>
                <p>Hold tight to your loved ones in the face</p>
                <p>Of bookended</p>
                <p>Eternity.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <style>
        .poem p {
            font-style: italic;
            font-size: 1.125rem;
            line-height: 1.8;
            margin: 0;
            padding-left: 1.6em;
            text-indent: -1.6em;
        }
        @media (max-width: 640px) {
            .poem p {
                font-size: 1.0625rem;
                line-height: 1.7;
            }
        }
    </style>

</BaseLayout>
